<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 26,203,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 26,203,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 04/16/97    04/09/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 26,203,000  25,938,000    25,759,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  63,762     116,421	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  35,324,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,516,775	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   04/16/97    04/09/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,358,000   4,234,000     4,458,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    4,619,000   4,826,000     4,095,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,184,000   3,846,000     4,173,000</p>
<p> South Central    2,220,000   2,388,000     2,853,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,767,000   3,824,000     3,332,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,997,000   5,051,000     5,068,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  2,058,000   1,768,000     1,780,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	26,203,000  25,938,000    25,759,000</p>
